---
  order = "13"
  doc = "Euclid's algorithm — the shape a real algorithm has: a recursive function
whose base case is a comparison and whose step is a remainder. The parameter is a
pair template, so each call unifies its argument with a fresh clone. The arrow's
compound domain states the same detailed template, while the recursive result's
type follows from the signature (`6: Int`). Nothing carries the `raw` mark,
because the type is decided."
  output = "6: Int"
---
gcd := ((p <: (@any : Int, @any : Int)) => if p(1) == 0 then p(0) else gcd (p(1), p(0) % p(1))) : (@any : Int, @any : Int) -> Int
gcd (48, 18)
